      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is that on 5.10 we don\u0027t have sched_cpu_util() function - so I had to pull it. But on 5.15 nd 6.1 this function is defined in core.c; so it only depends on CONFIG_SMP.\nBut when I tried to pull up the patches from Viresh that introduced this function, there were conflicts that made me uncomfortable to deal with without more additional testing to verify I don\u0027t accidentally break other things. so I opted to just pull in this function - but it relies on schedutil_cpu_util() function which is defined in cpufreq_schedutil.c instead of core.c like it is in 5.15 and 6.1. This means for 5.10 we need to depend on CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL.\n\nI expanded the commit message and pushed an updated patch that I did verify it builds against the reported config now.",
